+# System Interaction and Dependency Map
+
+## Purpose
+
+Identify the minimum integrated state required for living humor and folklore to emerge from the same causal world as Firstlight, unique casts, the Continuance Crawler, professions, media, institutions and distant civilizations.
+
+# 1. Core Causal Spine
+
+```text
+world event or social claim
+→ observer knowledge and privacy envelope
+→ memetic feature extraction
+→ bounded candidate genome
+→ creator agency and cultural grammar
+→ artifact or no artifact
+→ real distribution channel
+→ exposure, adoption or rejection
+→ mutation and meaning drift
+→ fatigue, decay, revival or folklore
+→ Chronicle and archaeological evidence
+```
+
+# 2. Required Dependencies
+
+## World Truth
+
+Chronicle events, objects, people, places, institutions and causal ancestry.
+
+## Observer Truth
+
+Witnesses, claims, confidence, communication and privacy.
+
+## Unique Cast
+
+Persistent identities, relationships, schedules, professions, voices, boundaries and creative skills.
+
+## Cultural State
+
+Household, neighborhood, profession, generation, faction, language, species and body cultures.
+
+## Distribution
+
+Conversation, workplace, physical objects, media, travel, Atlas routes and archives.
+
+## Safety
+
+Consent, power, target, sponsor, reach, content settings, moderation and repair.
+
+## Presentation
+
+Attention director, cognitive load, accessibility and character knowledge.
+
+# 3. Firstlight and Continuance Inputs
+
+The initial proof depends on:
+
+- generated residents;
+- Bent Feeder work;
+- warning and preparation history;
+- evacuation loading;
+- survivor ledger;
+- crawler cargo, sounds and interior objects;
+- private IRIS history;
+- post-title repair and social life.
+
+Meme ecology reads these states. It does not create substitute history.
+
+# 4. Symthaea Integration
+
+Symthaea may:
+
+- detect eligible events;
+- schedule low-cost candidate evaluation;
+- curate presentation opportunities;
+- protect contrast and suppress overload;
+- promote historical artifacts into detailed play.
+
+Symthaea may not:
+
+- alter event truth;
+- create harm for content;
+- publish private facts;
+- force creator participation;
+- guarantee audience adoption;
+- use account telemetry as an in-world source.
+
+# 5. IRIS Integration
+
+IRIS depends on:
+
+- player-known facts;
+- private shared-history tokens;
+- presentation preferences;
+- current pressure;
+- disclosure scope.
+
+IRIS output can become public culture only through a valid witness, recording or publication event.
+
+# 6. Muse and Media Integration
+
+Muse receives approved event, voice, motif and rights state.
+
+Media creation depends on:
+
+- creator skills and tools;
+- source assets;
+- rights and consent;
+- physical production where applicable;
+- accessibility alternatives;
+- deterministic hashes.
+
+Architecture and object memes also depend on labor, materials, ownership and maintenance.
+
+# 7. Information Ecology Integration
+
+Memes may carry claims, but expression and truth remain separate.
+
+```text
+what happened
+≠ what a witness believed
+≠ what a meme implies
+≠ what an audience concludes
+≠ what an institution publishes
+```
+
+Corrections may change belief without deleting the artifact or consequences.
+
+# 8. Harm and Justice Integration
+
+Harmful spread feeds:
+
+- reputation;
+- relationships;
+- employment;
+- migration;
+- justice;
+- platform policy;
+- propaganda;
+- repair.
+
+Targets retain independent response. The player is not guaranteed central authority.
+
+# 9. Time and Network Integration
+
+Interplanetary and interstellar culture depends on:
+
+- emission and reception time;
+- light delay or Atlas latency;
+- route availability;
+- archive custody;
+- translation;
+- local generation during isolation.
+
+Disconnected worlds develop divergent lineages.
+
+# 10. Simulation Fidelity
+
+## Full Detail
+
+Specific creators, expressions, exposures and objects.
+
+## Social Detail
+
+Group-level circulation, promoted creators and meaning state.
+
+## Historical Detail
+
+Variant families, institutions, durable media and conflicts.
+
+## Archival Detail
+
+Lineage, surviving evidence, disputed origin and revival predicates.
+
+Demotion may compress exposure history but must preserve unique artifacts, harmful campaigns, player-specific objects and branch points.
+
+# 11. Save, Replay and Multiplayer
+
+Authoritative state includes:
+
+- meme and variant ids;
+- source event ids;
+- creator;
+- expression hash;
+- lineage;
+- exposure summaries;
+- meaning by constituency;
+- privacy and moderation state;
+- media assets;
+- worldline binding.
+
+Clients do not independently regenerate public artifacts.
+
+# 12. Failure Chains
+
+Reject these chains:
+
+```text
+player telemetry → NPC joke
+private clinical event → public meme
+world truth → audience knowledge without channel
+random caption → culture
+high generation score → guaranteed virality
+harmful content → engagement reward
+branch event → another worldline’s folklore
+```
+
+# 13. Minimum Integrated Proof
+
+```text
+one Firstlight cast seed
++ twelve source events
++ eight cultural voices
++ one private IRIS token
++ one physical crawler object
++ one machine artifact
++ one Muse motif
++ one failed meme
++ one harmful conversion and repair path
++ one delayed route
++ seven-day recall
+```
+
+## Map Maxim
+
+> **The meme engine is downstream of truth, people and infrastructure. If it can generate culture without them, it is not integrated into Symtropy.**
