+# Symtropy Game Implementation Roadmap
+
+## Strategy
+
+Meme ecology does not replace the v2.7 vertical-slice priority. It attaches to the smallest proven Firstlight and Continuance event stream only after movement, one physical interaction, unique residents and authoritative history exist.
+
+# Gate A — Preserve the v2.7 Spine
+
+Continue movement, Bent Feeder, unique cast, warning, Breaking, evacuation and crawler work.
+
+**Exit:** authoritative source events and observers exist without meme systems.
+
+# Gate B — Event and Observer Trace
+
+Implement source-event envelopes, witness knowledge, privacy scopes and debug explanations.
+
+**Exit:** the system can prove what a potential creator knew.
+
+# Gate C — Deterministic Text Foundry
+
+Implement five authored frames, three voices, creator refusal, no-artifact outcomes and hashes.
+
+**Exit:** fixed fixtures reproduce exact candidates and rejections.
+
+# Gate D — Local Culture Only
+
+Implement face-to-face, household, workplace and one physical-sign channel.
+
+**Exit:** one phrase spreads locally without appearing globally.
+
+# Gate E — Selection and Fatigue
+
+Implement adoption, rejection, limited mutation, repetition detection, dormancy and one revival.
+
+**Exit:** strong candidates can fail and weak artifacts can disappear.
+
+# Gate F — Player and IRIS Boundaries
+
+Implement one player-specific event, one private IRIS callback, noncentrality budget and privacy tests.
+
+**Exit:** private content remains private and most culture concerns the world rather than the player.
+
+# Gate G — Safety Proof
+
+Implement consent state, clinical exclusion, harassment pattern, sponsor trace, hostile-content summarization and one repair path.
+
+**Exit:** harmful conversion remains legible without overpresentation.
+
+# Gate H — Multimodal Proof
+
+Implement one sign, one Muse motif, one gesture, one object label and accessibility alternatives.
+
+**Exit:** forms are culturally and materially distinct rather than caption duplicates.
+
+# Gate I — Network and History
+
+Implement route delay, lineage, historical aggregation, fatigue, extinction and revival.
+
+**Exit:** disconnected regions diverge and reconnect without chronology errors.
+
+# Gate J — Meme Ecology Benchmark
+
+Run twelve seeds, blind voice classification, safety review, performance profiling and seven-day delayed recall.
+
+**Exit:** promotion gates pass with no critical privacy or identity errors.
+
+# Deferred
+
+- open-ended image and video generation;
+- hundreds of faction grammars;
+- galaxy-wide live feeds;
+- player monetization or virality systems;
+- broad alien media generation;
+- architectural meme construction tools;
+- large propaganda simulation;
+- commercial creator economy.
+
+# Kill Rules
+
+- Cut generated media before cutting provenance.
+- Cut artifact count before allowing repetition.
+- Use authored templates before accepting identity errors.
+- Disable player-specific generation if it feels invasive.
+- Stop expansion if players remember captions but not source events or people.
+- Keep meme ecology out of the critical path if it threatens movement, interaction or cast work.
+- Prefer no joke over a privacy leak, cultural flattening or forced quip.
+
+## Roadmap Maxim
+
+> **First build a world worth remembering. Then prove that one household can turn one remembered event into one joke that still belongs to them.**
