+
+# v2.8 Meme Ecology, Cultural Mutation, Humor, and Living Folklore Campaign
+
+## Campaign Question
+
+Can Symtropy generate effectively endless humor by transforming real worldline memory into situated culture rather than by emitting random jokes or engagement feed content?
+
+## Canonical Decisions
+
+1. Memes originate in events, beliefs, artifacts or prior culture.
+2. Creation, adoption, spread and virality are separate states.
+3. Humor grammar belongs to people, professions, generations, factions and species.
+4. Most candidate jokes are rejected, unmade, ignored or forgotten.
+5. Spread requires actual contact and respects delay and isolation.
+6. Mutation preserves authoritative lineage.
+7. Player-specific memes require witnesses and worldline facts.
+8. IRIS private humor remains bounded by knowledge, pressure and disclosure.
+9. Symthaea may curate culture but may not manufacture suffering for content.
+10. Harm retains power, target, consent, sponsor, platform and repair state.
+11. Memes may live in text, music, gestures, objects, tools, architecture, machines and alien media.
+12. The experience rejects an endless global feed.
+13. Cultural history may outlive the original joke and forget its origin.
+14. Firstlight and Continuance remain the first implementation substrate.
+
+## Patch Sequence
+
+1. Meme ecology and living folklore contract.
+2. Event extraction, genome and Foundry runtime.
+3. Cultural humor grammar atlas.
+4. Mutation, distribution, decay and provenance runtime.
+5. Player-specific memes and IRIS private jokes.
+6. Harm, propaganda, harassment, consent and repair contract.
+7. Multimodal, Muse, gesture, architecture and translation runtime.
+8. Meme archaeology and folklore anthology.
+9. Benchmark, schemas, fixture and 100-ticket backlog.
+10. Registry and production integration.
+
+## First Production Promise
+
+The initial proof should let a player say:
+
+- “That joke came from something that happened in my world.”
+- “It sounded like the people who made it.”
+- “Not everything became content.”
+- “IRIS remembered one private thing without becoming annoying.”
+- “The joke changed when another group used it.”
+- “I understood why one version became harmful.”
+- “A week later, I remember the event as well as the phrase.”
+
+## Evidence Boundary
+
+This campaign is documentation evidence only. No meme generation, cultural distinction, media creation, propagation, safety, recall or performance claim is implemented by these files.
+
+## Campaign Maxim
+
+> **The living-world joke is not written above history. It is one of the ways history learns to travel through people.**
